{
  "id": null,
  "uid": "home-server-uptime",
  "title": "Home server — uptime and certificates",
  "description": "Synthetic probes from blackbox.nix. NOTE: these run ON the box being probed, so they do not prove internet reachability — they prove NPM routes, the certificates are valid and not expiring, and the public DNS records still resolve. Edit modules/nixos/server/dashboards/uptime.json.",
  "tags": ["nixos", "blackbox"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": false,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": { "from": "now-7d", "to": "now" },
  "templating": { "list": [] },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What these probes mean",
      "gridPos": { "h": 3, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "id": 90,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The prober runs **on this box**, so a green panel does not prove the service is reachable from the internet — a request to a public hostname either hairpins through the router or never leaves at all. What is proven: NPM terminates TLS with a valid certificate for each hostname and routes to the right backend, the certificates are not about to expire, and Cloudflare still serves the DNS records `cloudflare-ddns` publishes."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Certificate expiry",
      "description": "Days until the earliest certificate in the chain expires. Let's Encrypt issues for 90 days and NPM renews at 30 — so a value drifting below 21 means renewal has stopped working.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 3 },
      "id": 1,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "(probe_ssl_earliest_cert_expiry - time()) / 86400",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "d",
          "decimals": 1,
          "noValue": "no probe",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "orange", "value": 14 },
              { "color": "yellow", "value": 21 },
              { "color": "green", "value": 30 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": true }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Proxy routing",
      "description": "A request to 127.0.0.1:443 carrying the real hostname as SNI and Host — the whole NPM chain, TLS termination and backend routing included. Proxy hosts live in NPM's UI, not in Nix, so this is the only thing watching them.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 8, "y": 3 },
      "id": 2,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "probe_success{job=~\"probe-tls-.*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "no probe",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": { "text": "FAILING", "color": "red", "index": 1 },
                "1": { "text": "ok", "color": "green", "index": 0 }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "text", "value": null }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": true }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Public DNS",
      "description": "An AAAA lookup for each public hostname against a public resolver. cloudflare-ddns republishes the box's IPv6 every five minutes; this is what shows a stalled updater or a deleted record.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 16, "y": 3 },
      "id": 3,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "probe_success{job=~\"probe-dns-.*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "no probe",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": { "text": "NOT RESOLVING", "color": "red", "index": 1 },
                "1": { "text": "ok", "color": "green", "index": 0 }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "text", "value": null }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": true }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Certificate lifetime remaining",
      "description": "The sawtooth is renewal working: each issue resets the line to 90 days. A line that keeps falling through 30 is a renewal that did not happen.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 8 },
      "id": 10,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "(probe_ssl_earliest_cert_expiry - time()) / 86400",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "d",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never", "lineWidth": 2 },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 14 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "min"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Probe success",
      "description": "Every probe, one line each. Gaps are Prometheus not scraping; zeros are the probe running and failing — the two mean different things.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 8 },
      "id": 11,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "probe_success",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}} — {{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "decimals": 0,
          "custom": { "fillOpacity": 20, "showPoints": "never", "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "lastNotNull"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Probe duration",
      "description": "How long each probe took. A climbing line on the TLS probes is usually the backend getting slow, not the proxy.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 16 },
      "id": 12,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "probe_duration_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}} — {{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "fillOpacity": 0, "showPoints": "never", "lineWidth": 2 }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "HTTP status returned",
      "description": "What the proxy actually answered. A 502 here with a green systemd unit is the classic \"backend moved, NPM still points at the old port\".",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 16 },
      "id": 13,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "probe_http_status_code",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}} — {{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 0,
          "custom": { "fillOpacity": 0, "showPoints": "always", "lineWidth": 1 }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      }
    }
  ]
}
